Sure! Below is a minimal example of an **HTML card** that **rotates** (spins) when you hover over it.  
It uses only CSS (no JavaScript).  

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Hover‑Rotate Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body{
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    min-height:100vh;
    margin:0;
    background:#f0f0f0;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card{
    width:260px;          /* width of the card */
    height:360px;         /* height of the card */
    perspective:800px;    /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
    cursor:pointer;       /* hand icon on hover */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Inner wrapper that actually rotates ---------- */
.card-inner{
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transform-style:preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
    transition:transform .6s ease; /* smooth animation */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card-inner{
    transform:rotateY(180deg);     /* rotate 180° around Y axis */
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card-face{
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;    /* hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
}

.card-front{
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.card-back{
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* place it behind the front */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

/* ---------- 6️⃣ Sample content styling ---------- */
h2{
    margin:0 0 10px;
    font-size:1.4rem;
}
p{
    margin:0;
    color:#555;
}
```

