<body>

<div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
        <!-- Front face -->
        <div class="card-face card-front">
            <h2>Front Side</h2>
            <p>Hover over me!</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back face -->
        <div class="card-face card-back">
            <h2>Back Side</h2>
            <p>Thanks for hovering.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| 1 | The `.card` element sets `perspective`, giving depth to the 3D rotation. |
| 2 | `.card-inner` holds both faces and has `transform-style: preserve-3d` so its children stay in 3D space. |
| 3 | On hover, we rotate `.card-inner` by 180° around the Y‑axis. |
| 4 | Each face (`.card-face`) has `backface-visibility:hidden` so the hidden side disappears during rotation. |
| 5 | The back face is pre‑rotated 180° so it appears correctly after the parent rotates. |

Feel free to replace the sample text, images, or colors with your own design. If you need a different rotation axis (e.g., X‑axis for flipping up/down), just change `rotateY(180deg)` to `rotateX(180deg)` (and adjust the back face accordingly). Enjoy!
